# Acta env — single Next.js app. Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# SECRET BOUNDARY: only variables prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are inlined into the
# browser bundle. Everything else is server-only (route handlers, Server
# Components, server actions) and must NEVER be given a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# Server-only modules should also `import "server-only"` as a hard guard.

# For LOCAL dev, point these at the local Supabase stack (`supabase start`):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:54321"
#   and the anon / service_role keys that `supabase start` prints.
# For the DEPLOYED app, use the hosted project's values (set them in the deploy
# platform's env, not here). Magic-link sign-in is the only auth method; locally
# the email is captured in the mail inbox `supabase start` prints (~:54324).

# --- Public (safe to ship to the browser) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:54321"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-local-or-project-anon-key"

# --- Server-only (NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_; never sent to the client) ---
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-local-or-project-service-role-key"

# LLM provider keys for the Extract agent (U4) — server-only.
OPENAI_API_KEY=""
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# --- Optional: RLS isolation integration test (auto-skips if unset) ---
# Set to the local stack values to run src/server/rls.integration.test.ts.
# SUPABASE_TEST_URL="http://127.0.0.1:54321"
# SUPABASE_TEST_ANON_KEY=""
# SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""
